{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_092df2b58322bc5b0db1807afeea6943b7cfdcb411ddb0f68adab51406f7b4b7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI is invoked as `cs` with subcommands including completion, debug, help, reset, and version, plus flags like --autoyes and --program."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4fc6e84aa2b46ee403a7ecbf24736f6bfca79214ba07886e912ea130eaca3f2a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product requires tmux and the GitHub CLI (gh) as prerequisites."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5c82fe4ca46b5ab66e1f81c45f62240767ab8507bb10bfa4c82aea8e29f36f76"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"When no profiles are defined, the app uses `default_program` directly as the launch command, defaulting to `claude`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_711115868d893aa61ac071c5bf63b3a281fd1da0050acbcd8dd73c87aab2c3df"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Claude Squad is a terminal application that manages multiple local AI coding agents such as Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, and Aider in separate workspaces for parallel tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_87fa88b518a1a8d3f6b426cf0bb27a06902e993999f3aee5cbd238108a4f72e1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app uses tmux for isolated per-agent terminal sessions and git worktrees so each session works on its own branch, with a TUI for navigation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ce9e1559ffd1d59cfae0f909159c1c503f6688c82e50994060f220ae5a4f55f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is stored in `~/.claude-squad/config.json`, and the exact path can be found via `cs debug`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a05a6ed103a32d9e76cb1cc9d13c11420b416513972d622c55262b5bbc62428c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Profiles allow named program configurations selectable at session creation; a `profiles` array with name/program fields and `default_program` is set in the config file."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a7a576cc5d4dbd0b750ed866770788ffc74a0c575e71acfdd3dbdfa63dc8a725"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The `-p/--program` flag lets users launch a chosen agent command in new instances, e.g. `cs -p \"codex\"` or an aider command with a specific model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b7dad2ea275be19f97b0732252b4ea4997f0fcf395afcb4b914787055811e1c1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An experimental `-y/--autoyes` flag makes all instances automatically accept prompts for Claude Code and Aider; the README also mentions background yolo/auto-accept mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ec68ea97733d3e9f6bf9e6118d1fcc6e9c3f74de0dc4656a8e5937bea7e7874c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Keybindings support session creation (`n`, `N`), deletion (`D`), attach/detach (`↵/o`, ctrl-q), commit-push (`s`), checkout (`c`), resume (`r`), and diff-view navigation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_092df2b58322bc5b0db1807afeea6943b7cfdcb411ddb0f68adab51406f7b4b7","clm_4fc6e84aa2b46ee403a7ecbf24736f6bfca79214ba07886e912ea130eaca3f2a","clm_5c82fe4ca46b5ab66e1f81c45f62240767ab8507bb10bfa4c82aea8e29f36f76","clm_711115868d893aa61ac071c5bf63b3a281fd1da0050acbcd8dd73c87aab2c3df","clm_87fa88b518a1a8d3f6b426cf0bb27a06902e993999f3aee5cbd238108a4f72e1","clm_8ce9e1559ffd1d59cfae0f909159c1c503f6688c82e50994060f220ae5a4f55f","clm_a05a6ed103a32d9e76cb1cc9d13c11420b416513972d622c55262b5bbc62428c","clm_a7a576cc5d4dbd0b750ed866770788ffc74a0c575e71acfdd3dbdfa63dc8a725","clm_b7dad2ea275be19f97b0732252b4ea4997f0fcf395afcb4b914787055811e1c1","clm_ec68ea97733d3e9f6bf9e6118d1fcc6e9c3f74de0dc4656a8e5937bea7e7874c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_761875c9fd34461c962d578ff399bf0d","id":"pg_0a012e726f8f58fc9706a58f6f278637","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/smtg-ai-claude-squad-readme-md-ce1ffb4392b0-a58f6f278637.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c7c41fc7632d5b258cc6d29ce33b666e"],"title":"smtg-ai/claude-squad/README.md @ ce1ffb4392b0","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_761875c9fd34461c962d578ff399bf0d"}
